<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Glimm et al. (2014) & Ho et al. (2019) avian feather bud hexagonal array, EDA traveling competence wave & FGF20/BMP4 perturbations — Model fidelity to source: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Faithfully implements Glimm et al. (2014) and Ho et al. (2019) coupled 2D Keller-Segel dermal chemotaxis + FGF20 chemoattractant + BMP4 lateral inhibitor PDEs under a bilateral mediolateral EDA competence wave s_w(x,t) (L223-366), linear stability dispersion and critical chemotactic threshold chi_c = 0.0540 (L107-159), half-period BMP4 saddle phase pinning (Delta_y = lambda_y/2, Delta_x = (sqrt(3)/2)*lambda_y), V-shaped bilateral space-time kymograph (Panel D, matching Ho et al. 2019 Fig. 4D), and all 5 experimental regimes (WT wave, Fc-chEDA1 simultaneous competence, Ecto-D2 narrowed wave, *scaleless* FGF20-null, and Latrunculin motility blockade). Backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
